      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Wherever the catalog fully covers a chore, a catalog-told agent produces bytes IDENTICAL to the engine (3/3 chores) at ~30% fewer output tokens than bare hands \u2014 and the raw engine does it for $0 in seconds with zero variance and byte-clean reversibility. Untold agents (A\u2032) hand-edited 2/2 with the tool on disk: the reminder IS the mechanism, so it is now wired into the epic-cycle builder prompts themselves (1860a7097)."
        }
      ],
      "id": "sls-013",
      "title": "The headline, measured",
      "tone": "success",
      "type": "callout"
    },
    {
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Dollar separation is cache-dominated (~$0.55 spawn floor) on small chores; partial coverage taxes users into hand-top-ups (measured on ensure-cli-noun, fixed structurally the same day); the boundary chore leaked its staging and P4 is inconclusive as registered. Full detail: /papers/scaffy-benchmark."
        }
      ],
      "id": "sls-014",
      "title": "The honest boundaries",
      "tone": "warning",
      "type": "callout"
